      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 3 and 6, we list the factors of each number and identify the common factors:\n\n- Factors of 3: 1, 3\n- Factors of 6: 1, 2, 3, 6\n\nThe common factors are 1 and 3. The greatest common factor is 3.\n\nNext, to find the least common multiple (LCM) of 3 and 6, we list the multiples of each number and identify the smallest multiple that is common:\n\n- Multiples of 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, ...\n- Multiples of 6: 6, 12, 18, 24, ...\n\nThe smallest multiple that is common to both lists is 6. Therefore, the least common multiple is 6.\n\nFinally, we add the GCF and the LCM:\n\n3 (GCF) + 6 (LCM) = 9\n\nTherefore, the sum of the greatest common factor of 3 and 6 and the least common multiple of 3 and 6 is 9.",
