      "text": "To find the sum of the greatest common factor (GCF) of 3 and 6 and the least common multiple (LCM) of 3 and 6, we first need to determine both values.\n\n1. **Finding the GCF of 3 and 6:**\n   - The factors of 3 are 1 and 3.\n   - The factors of 6 are 1, 2, 3, and 6.\n   - The common factors of 3 and 6 are 1 and 3.\n   - The greatest common factor (GCF) is the largest of these common factors, which is 3.\n   - Therefore, the GCF of 3 and 6 is 3.\n\n2. **Finding the LCM of 3 and 6:**\n   - The multiples of 3 are 3, 6, 9, 12, ...\n   - The multiples of 6 are 6, 12, 18, ...\n   - The smallest common multiple of 3 and 6 is 6.\n   - Therefore, the LCM of 3 and 6 is 6.\n\n3. **Summing the GCF and the LCM:**\n   - We have found that the GCF of 3 and 6 is 3.\n   - We have also found that the LCM of 3 and 6 is 6.\n   - The sum of the GCF and the LCM is \\(3 + 6 = 9\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
